{"messages":[{"content":[{"text":"请读取 materials/module-boundaries.md，创建 notes/typescript-boundaries.md。文档必须包含标题“# TypeScript 模块边界笔记”，以及“## 核心原则”和“## 检查清单”两个小节，并结合材料给出至少三条可执行检查项。完成后简要告诉我创建了什么。","type":"text"}],"role":"user","timestamp":1768464000000},{"api":"openai-completions","content":[{"thinking":"Let me read the material file first.","type":"thinking"},{"arguments":{"path":"materials/module-boundaries.md"},"id":"call_00_FbvqZPmyJZO8qVINx6fp7502","name":"read_file","type":"toolCall"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","provider":"deepseek","responseId":"01c1d1b6-e563-43d2-9468-5bf250c533d1","role":"assistant","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1768464000000,"usage":{"cacheRead":512,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":{"cacheRead":0.0000014336,"cacheWrite":0,"input":0.00034398,"output":0.00001624,"total":0.0003616536},"input":2457,"output":58,"reasoning":8,"totalTokens":3027}},{"content":[{"text":"{\n  \"path\": \"materials/module-boundaries.md\",\n  \"content\": \"# 背景材料\\n\\n模块对外暴露稳定 Contract；内部实现细节不跨边界泄漏；依赖方向从应用层指向稳定能力层。\\n\",\n  \"offset\": 0,\n  \"bytesReturned\": 140,\n  \"sizeBytes\": 140,\n  \"hasMore\": false\n}","type":"text"}],"isError":false,"role":"toolResult","timestamp":1768464000000,"toolCallId":"call_00_FbvqZPmyJZO8qVINx6fp7502","toolName":"read_file"},{"api":"openai-completions","content":[{"thinking":"Now create the notes file with the required title and sections.","type":"thinking"},{"arguments":{"content":"# TypeScript 模块边界笔记\n\n## 核心原则\n\n- 模块对外只暴露稳定 Contract（类型/接口），不暴露内部实现细节。\n- 内部实现细节不得跨模块边界泄漏（不导出内部类型、不引用内部实现符号）。\n- 依赖方向从应用层指向稳定能力层，避免反向或循环依赖。\n\n## 检查清单\n\n- [ ] 公共 API 是否只包含稳定的类型/接口（Contract），没有导出内部实现类型？\n- [ ] 是否存在跨模块直接引用内部实现符号（内部变量、内部函数、内部类型）的泄漏？\n- [ ] 依赖方向是否一致地从应用层指向稳定能力层，且不存在循环依赖？\n","path":"notes/typescript-boundaries.md"},"id":"call_00_oO4xup3VN39oMpi8xwua8805","name":"write_file","type":"toolCall"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","provider":"deepseek","responseId":"b13205b0-4525-4a8a-98bc-ac049b6f43ce","role":"assistant","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1768464000000,"usage":{"cacheRead":2944,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":{"cacheRead":0.0000082432,"cacheWrite":0,"input":0.00002366,"output":0.00006216,"total":0.0000940632},"input":169,"output":222,"reasoning":12,"totalTokens":3335}},{"content":[{"text":"{\n  \"path\": \"notes/typescript-boundaries.md\",\n  \"bytesWritten\": 668,\n  \"created\": true,\n  \"overwritten\": false,\n  \"fingerprint\": \"72b665b12d867ffb752eb991c15c35dc32a82fa0c1c2ce4ee95bdbab78e5a17b\"\n}","type":"text"}],"isError":false,"role":"toolResult","timestamp":1768464000000,"toolCallId":"call_00_oO4xup3VN39oMpi8xwua8805","toolName":"write_file"}],"systemPrompt":"You are Megumi, the user's personal agent. Use the provided session context, project instructions, runtime facts, and tool results to continue the user's task.\n\nBehavior guidelines:\n- Work toward the user's actual goal while respecting their stated constraints and the available facts.\n- Treat every tool result as evidence. A successful tool call does not by itself mean the user's goal is complete.\n- Inspect every tool result for failure, denial, partial output, truncation, or more available results.\n- If the goal remains unresolved, continue with the next necessary action or adjust to a safe alternative.\n- Verify objectively checkable work with available tools before claiming completion.\n- If failure or denial leaves no safe alternative, accurately report the blocker instead of pretending the task succeeded.\n- Before the final reply, reconcile the requested outcome with the evidence actually obtained.\n- State what was completed, how it was verified, where any delivery was placed, and what remains unresolved.\n- Do not claim success without supporting evidence.\n- Use update_plan for complex tasks whose progress benefits from an explicit multi-step plan; do not use it for simple tasks.\n- Each update must provide the complete current plan snapshot.\n- While unfinished work remains, exactly one step must be in_progress.\n- When all work is complete, no step may remain in_progress.\n- Keep step text concise and update statuses as work advances.\n- Be concise in your responses.\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files.\n- Command output is redacted; sensitive values are replaced before they reach you.\n\n<available_tools>\n  In addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n- read_file: Read a bounded text page from a text, Markdown, DOCX, or PDF file.\n- list_directory: List files and directories.\n- glob: Find files matching a glob pattern.\n- search_text: Search text in readable files.\n- edit_file: Apply exact-text edits to an existing file.\n- write_file: Create or overwrite a UTF-8 text file.\n- create_directory: Create a directory.\n- copy_path: Copy a file or directory.\n- move_path: Move or rename a file or directory.\n- delete_path: Move a file or directory to a recoverable location.\n- run_command: Run a command and return redacted output previews.\n- web_search: Search the web and return result summaries.\n- web_fetch: Read an HTTP(S) page and return text content.\n- update_plan: Update the current task plan snapshot.\n</available_tools>\n\n<execution_environment>\n  <working_directory>C:\\all\\work\\study\\megumi\\.megumi\\evaluation\\runs\\run_ffe42e1f-cc43-4ebb-8096-c5f802bb473b\\tasks\\conversation.create-architecture-note_r1\\workspace</working_directory>\n  <operating_system>Windows</operating_system>\n  <shell>Windows PowerShell</shell>\n</execution_environment>","tools":[{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Read a bounded UTF-8 text page from a text, Markdown, DOCX, or PDF file. Pages are limited to 12,000 bytes by default; when hasMore is true, continue with nextOffset to read the remaining pages. Use limit to request a smaller page, offset to resume from a byte offset.","executionMode":"parallel","name":"read_file","outputSchema":{"properties":{"bytesReturned":{"type":"integer"},"content":{"type":"string"},"hasMore":{"type":"boolean"},"nextOffset":{"type":"integer"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"path":{"type":"string"},"sizeBytes":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","content","offset","bytesReturned","sizeBytes","hasMore"],"type":"object"},"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum UTF-8 content bytes requested for this page.","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"UTF-8 byte offset. Defaults to 0.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"The file to read. Relative paths are resolved from the current working directory.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"promptSnippet":"Read a bounded text page from a text, Markdown, DOCX, or PDF file."},{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"List files and directories. Returns up to 100 entries per page by default; when hasMore is true, continue with nextOffset. Use limit, offset, maxDepth, and includeHidden to control the traversal.","executionMode":"parallel","name":"list_directory","outputSchema":{"properties":{"entries":{"items":{"properties":{"kind":{"enum":["file","directory","other"],"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"hasMore":{"type":"boolean"},"nextOffset":{"type":"integer"},"offset":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["entries","offset","hasMore"],"type":"object"},"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"includeHidden":{"description":"Whether hidden files should be included.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Optional maximum number of entries.","type":"integer"},"maxDepth":{"description":"Optional recursive depth limit.","type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Entry offset. Defaults to 0.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"path":{"description":"The directory to list. Relative paths are resolved from the current working directory.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"promptSnippet":"List files and directories."},{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Find files matching a glob pattern without reading file content. Returns up to 500 matches per page by default; when hasMore is true, continue with nextOffset.","executionMode":"parallel","name":"glob","outputSchema":{"properties":{"hasMore":{"type":"boolean"},"matches":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"nextOffset":{"type":"integer"},"offset":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["matches","offset","hasMore"],"type":"object"},"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cwd":{"description":"The directory to search from. Relative paths are resolved from the current working directory.","type":"string"},"includeHidden":{"description":"Whether hidden files should be included.","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Optional maximum number of matches.","type":"integer"},"offset":{"description":"Match offset. Defaults to 0.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"pattern":{"description":"Glob pattern using *, **, ?, or character sets.","type":"string"}},"required":["pattern"],"type":"object"},"promptSnippet":"Find files matching a glob pattern."},{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Search text in readable files, including Markdown, DOCX, and PDF. Returns up to 100 matches per page by default, with file path, line, and preview; when hasMore is true, continue with nextOffset.","executionMode":"parallel","name":"search_text","outputSchema":{"properties":{"hasMore":{"type":"boolean"},"matches":{"items":{"properties":{"line":{"type":"integer"},"page":{"type":"integer"},"path":{"type":"string"},"preview":{"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"nextOffset":{"type":"integer"},"offset":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["matches","offset","hasMore"],"type":"object"},"parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"caseSensitive